Subject: [PATCH] feat: Herbiboar tracking on Fossil Island
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Herbiboar tracking on Fossil Island was not implemented.

Change. Herbiboar tracking in the Mushroom Forest, driven by the
client's own trail varbits (the footprint multilocs on the map) so
RuneLite's Herbiboar plugin works: start locs (Hunter 80, boostable, and
31 Herblore), clue loc inspects (the wiki's messages, 50 XP and fossil
rolls), the tunnel (Hunter XP by level, from the base level; the stunned
herbiboar via fossil_herbiboar_visible) and the harvest (1-3 herbs, 2-4
with magic secateurs, by Herblore level from the wiki chart, 25
Herblore XP per herb after the first, harvest count). The network
(dbtables herbiboar_legs/spots/tunnels/herbs, 56006-56009, rows
60184-60270, own HerbiboarPluginPack) is read from the map's footprints
and the plugin's per-loc trail lists; server varps 63770-63771. Needs
the Hunter module skeleton PR.

Tests. Integration suite HerbiboarScriptTest (5): tunnel XP against the
wiki table, herb level ranges against the wiki chart, every leg's trail
varbit is a footprint varbit and every group can be left, tracking from
every start to stun and harvest, a wrong clue loc changes nothing.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Herbiboar (requirements, tunnel XP, fossil
table, herb chart, messages), Tunnel (herbiboar), Muddy patch, Smelly
mushroom. Trail varbits, multilocs and locs from the cache; RuneLite
Herbiboar plugin (BSD) for the per-loc trail lists.

Caveats. Guesses: route length (3-5 legs) and which legs end a route,
50 XP on every inspect but the first and last (the wiki says
"occasionally"), the seaweed and mushroom-cap messages and the other
non-wiki messages, the tunnel's Search op doing the same as Attack. Not
done: the new-track warning dialogue, the Herbi pet, the horn of
plenty's extra herbs.

